SOURCE READ that explains Q1 -- beanie/migrations/controllers/iterative.py:93-127

    async def run(self, session):
        output_documents = []
        all_migration_ops = []
        async for input_document in self.input_document_model.find_all(session=session):
            ...
            output_documents.append(output_document)
            if len(output_documents) == self.batch_size:          # batch_size default 10000 (line 45)
                all_migration_ops.append(
                    self.output_document_model.replace_many(documents=output_documents, session=session)
                )
                output_documents = []
        if output_documents:
            all_migration_ops.append(
                self.output_document_model.replace_many(documents=output_documents, session=session)
            )
        await asyncio.gather(*all_migration_ops)                   # <-- NOTHING is awaited until here

The replace_many coroutines are COLLECTED, not awaited, until the whole collection has
been transformed. So a failure in the transform writes nothing, at any collection size.
A failure inside the final gather is a different matter -- see the check's caveats.
